Suggests: culmus
Description: check IPTV and internet radio playlists for dead streams
 Desktop application for TV (IPTV) and internet radio playlists in M3U,
 M3U8, PLS and XSPF format. Playlists can be opened from files, from whole
 folders or from a web address.
 .
 Every stream is checked: HTTP/HTTPS, HLS (including the real video
 segment), Icecast and Shoutcast radio, RTMP, RTSP and MMS. Offline and
 broken channels can be rechecked, duplicates are marked, and groups can be
 included, excluded, renamed, merged and reordered.
 .
 A clean playlist is saved with channel logos, EPG data and player options
 kept, optionally as one playlist per group, together with a CSV report.
 Channels that only show a "not available in your country" banner are
 detected (server answer, looping placeholder, picture fingerprint with
 ffmpeg) and left out. Hebrew and other right-to-left channel names are
 displayed correctly.
